    "content_descriptors": {
      "ids": [
        5
      ],
      "notes": "Snap out. contains no sexual content, no nudity, no depictions of realistic violence or gore, and no drug or alcohol use.\r\n\r\nWhat it does contain is a sustained portrait of avoidance, and players may want to know what that looks like before starting:\r\n\r\nSelf-critical inner monologue. The narrator is the player character's own mind, and it comments on failure, avoidance and lost time in a harsh, repetitive register throughout the game.\r\n\r\nCompulsive scrolling and lost time. The central subject is losing hours to a social media feed. Players who struggle with compulsive phone or social media use may find this uncomfortable.\r\n\r\nFriendship breakdown and withdrawal. Five relationships can be neglected. Left long enough, a conversation ends for good \u2014 a character goes quiet, or the thread closes permanently.\r\n\r\nExhaustion and burnout. One of the game's endings frames the character as simply too tired to keep going.\r\n\r\nMild profanity. The word \"shitty\" appears in one character's conversation, inside reply options the player chooses.\r\n\r\nThere is no depiction of self-harm, suicide, sexual content, sexual violence, or real-world violence. The player character can die repeatedly in the platformer sections; these are abstract, non-graphic hazard deaths with no blood or gore."
    }
